{"id":"H3008","lemma":"יִגְאָל","transliteration":"yigal","sayIt":"yig-AL","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Igal","meaning":"A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.13.7;\nson of: Joseph (H3130H)\n§ Igal or Igeal = \"He redeems\"\n1) son of Joseph and a spy from the tribe of Issachar\n2) son of Nathan of Zobah, one of David's mighty warriors\n3) a son of Shemaiah and descendant of Zerubbabel","glosses":["igal"],"count":3,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"num-13","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"Igal","kjv":"Igal"}},{"chapterId":"2sa-23","v":36,"renderings":{"bsb":"Igal","kjv":"Igal"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-3","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"Igal","kjv":"and Igeal"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Numbers 13:7","note":"Of the tribe of Issachar, Igal the son of Joseph.","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Samuel 23:36","note":"Igal the son of Nathan of Zobah, Bani the Gadite,","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Chronicles 3:22","note":"The son of Shecaniah: Shemaiah. The sons of Shemaiah: Hattush, Igal, Bariah, Neariah, and Shaphat, six.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H1282","lemma":"בָּרִיחַ","transliteration":"bariach","gloss":"Bariah"},{"id":"H2407","lemma":"חַטּוּשׁ","transliteration":"chattush","gloss":"Hattush"},{"id":"H3130","lemma":"יוֹסֵף","transliteration":"yoseph","gloss":"Joseph"},{"id":"H5416","lemma":"נָתָן","transliteration":"natan","gloss":"Nathan"},{"id":"H8098","lemma":"שְׁמַעְיָ֫הוּ","transliteration":"shemayah","gloss":"Shemaiah"},{"id":"H5294","lemma":"נְעַרְיָה","transliteration":"nearyah","gloss":"Neariah"},{"id":"H8202","lemma":"שָׁפָט","transliteration":"shaphat","gloss":"Shaphat"}],"senses":[{"id":"H3008H","gloss":"Igal","relation":"H3008H ="},{"id":"H3008I","gloss":"Igal","relation":"H3008I ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}